        "text": "I think that's a solid explanation. I've verified both formulas with induction, and then connected them algebraically by considering the nature of even and odd numbers and their sums as arithmetic series."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "The sum of the first \\( n \\) odd numbers is \\( n^2 \\) and the sum of the first \\( n \\) even numbers is \\( n(n+1) \\)."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "The relationship between these two formulas is that the sum of the first \\( n \\) even numbers is equal to the sum of the first \\( n \\) odd numbers plus \\( n \\), which can be expressed as \\( n(n+1) = n^2 + n \\)."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Therefore, the relationship is \\boxed{n(n+1) = n^2 + n}."
      }
